cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum Anchor V1.2.4 — Tesseract Anchor Protocol and Measurement Ledger"
abstract: >-
  An experimental protocol for coherent state anchoring on superconducting QPUs,
  together with the measurement ledger that tests it. The original pulse-level
  protocol (qiskit.pulse, meas_level=0) was deprecated by IBM in 2024 and removed
  from production QPUs in February 2025. V1.2.4 migrates to working APIs and
  reports evidence grades honestly. Measured: single-qubit dynamics psi(37ns)=0.331662
  under a gamma=0 model on ibm_marrakesh; four independent Bell pairs at 95-96%
  per-plane balance on IQM Resonance Garnet 20Q; Tesseract-V2 inter-plane
  entangling backbone at 83.01% global 8-qubit GHZ coherence (850/1024, Wilson CI
  [80.59%, 85.18%], non-overlapping with V1 [9.80%, 13.73%]) — this establishes
  that plane coupling works. Documented negative results: the anchor-on and
  anchor-off conditions both yield 0% clear; the V1 global 8-qubit correlation is
  11.62%, consistent with statistically independent planes; and the Tesseract-V3
  five-phase interferometric hardware sweep (5/5 phases, IQM Garnet 20Q, 1024
  shots per phase, 2026-10-08) is noise-dominated — goodness-of-fit rejects the
  theoretical cos(8*phi) curve (chi2=30.72, df=4, p<0.0001) and cannot reject a
  flat response (chi2=1.98, df=4, p=0.7392), so the five phases are not
  statistically distinguishable and the cos(8*phi) modulation is NOT established
  on hardware. The physical anchor-drive compensation effect is NOT proven by any
  measurement in this work. An earlier positive result is retracted as a circuit
  tautology.
